course: dictionary
lesson: 15792
title: Unaided
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how something is done. Unaided is one of them. The un- at the start means "not", and aided means "helped", so unaided means not helped. «She climbed the tree unaided.» Nobody held the ladder or pulled her up. She did it alone.
explain: The word can also describe how you look at things. «Some planets can be seen with the unaided eye.» No telescope or microscope is needed, just your own eyes. The clue is the word eye: the sentence tells you what kind of help is missing.
explain: Teachers use it too. «Maya completed the maths test unaided.» That means she did all the work herself, with no help from a parent, friend, or teacher. When you meet a new word, ask yourself what was left out, then check your idea in the sentence.
fact: Unaided means without help from anyone or anything.
fact: The prefix un- means "not", so unaided means "not helped".
fact: «Unaided» can describe a person's actions: «She climbed the tree unaided.»
fact: With the unaided eye means without a telescope or microscope.
fact: Phrases you may see are walk unaided, unaided by, and completed unaided.
exercise: «Ben walked across the room unaided.» What does unaided mean here? | Very quickly | *Without any help | Carrying a heavy bag | With a friend holding his hand
exercise: Find and copy one word that tells you Lily had no help: «Lily finished her puzzle unaided.» | finished | *unaided | puzzle | Lily
exercise: Which sentence means you can see something without a telescope? | You need a telescope to see the craters on the Moon | *You can spot the brightest stars with the unaided eye | Sam looked through a microscope at a leaf | Dad peered through binoculars at a bird
test: «Grandma can cook dinner unaided now that her hands are stronger.» What does unaided mean? | Very quickly | *Without help | Using a microwave | With a recipe book open
test: Mrs Okoro writes "completed unaided" on Tom's spelling test. What does that tell you? | Tom copied the answers from a friend | Tom forgot his pencil | Tom finished early because the test was easy | *Tom did the test with no help
exam: Which word means not helped by anyone or anything? | Unkind | Unfair | *Unaided | Unwell
